    },
    {
      "speaker": "sam",
      "text": "By the end, the start is gone.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "the start gets lost",
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rao",
      "text": "Old language models read exactly like that. One word at a time, in order. They were called RNNs.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "RNN",
          "at": 0.75
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "RNN: one word at a time",
          "at": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "sam",
      "text": "So they forget, and they're slow.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "forgetful and slow",
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "In 2017, a team of researchers published a paper called Attention Is All You Need.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "clear"
        },
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "board-full"
        },
        {
          "do": "sketch.box",
          "id": "paper",
          "text": "Attention Is All You Need",
          "sub": "Vaswani et al., 2017",
          "icon": "cloud",
          "tone": "accent",
          "at": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "sam",
      "text": "So how does it stop the forgetting?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "sketch.note",
          "text": "how?",
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rao",
      "text": "Every word looks at every other word, and decides who matters.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "clear"
        },
        {
          "do": "layout",
          "template": "db-focus"
        },
        {
          "do": "db.table",
          "id": "att",
          "name": "The cat sat because it was tired",
          "columns": [
            "it looks at",
            "how much"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "cat",
              "a lot"
            ],
            [
              "tired",
              "some"
            ],
            [
              "sat",
              "a little"
            ]
          ],
          "at": 0.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "rao",
      "text": "Those scores are called attention weights. The model learns them from data.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "attention weights",
          "at": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "sam",
      "text": "So nothing gets whispered down a line anymore.",
      "visuals": []
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Better still, every word is handled at the same time. Training runs in parallel on GPUs.",
      "visuals": [
